 let mut md=format!("# Coupled Gaussian CIOS component\n\nComponent screen: **{}**. No production change or verified proof speedup. The original all-eight CPU10×goal remains unmet,0/8. This changes the Gaussian reduction recurrence while retaining the [parent headroom and lazy butterfly](../2026-10-27-gaussian-fr-headroom/README.md).\n\nThe base field uses two short Gaussian coordinates with six expanded vectors. Three coupled Montgomery cancellation rounds of52,52,26bits replace the full product and inverse convolution. Unsigned cancellation digits reconstruct the same Gaussian multiplier as the parent Comba oracle; the final digit identifies centering. Both input and modulus Gauss sum products need an explicit53-bit digit carry. Stored canonical coordinates remain32bytes; no proving-key table, duplicated plan, extra workers or C/assembly backend is introduced. This does not prove process memory equivalence.\n\n## Measurements\n\nRyzen9950X,CPU2,oneOSthread.31 fixed rotated/reversed fresh-process blocks,100000iterations after3×2000primes. The parent Comba binary is reused byte-exact as a contemporaneous control, alongside its ordinary field baseline. The new binary has unchanged ordinary field arithmetic, allowing a cross-binary calibration. Actual FFT field radix is2^260 with CIOS cancellation-carry enabled. Conversion is outside timing; one result-vector allocation is included. No owned helper/build/hash/archive/secondCPU workload overlaps capture.\n\n|Pattern|Label|Median ns/unit|\n|---|---|---:|\n",if passed{"pass"}else{"fail"});
